<div class="static-page">
  <section class="static-page__intro">
    <h1>How Tempasi works</h1>
    <p class="static-page__subtitle">
      A short walkthrough of the catalog, buying vs. renting, and the
      cabinet.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="static-page__section">
    <h2>Browsing templates</h2>
    <p>
      The <a href="/templates">catalog</a> lists every available template.
      Templates that are currently rented or already sold as exclusive are
      shown as unavailable — you're never buying or renting something
      someone else is already using.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="static-page__section">
    <h2>Buy vs. Rent</h2>
    <div class="static-page__grid">
      <article class="static-page__card">
        <h3>Buy</h3>
        <p>
          A one-time purchase. The template is yours, permanently removed
          from the catalog for other buyers.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="static-page__card">
        <h3>Rent</h3>
        <p>
          A temporary exclusivity hold, priced for the period you need. If
          you later decide to buy the same template, the unused value of an
          active rental converts into Tempasi credit and is applied to the
          purchase automatically.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="static-page__section">
    <h2>The Cabinet</h2>
    <p>
      Everything related to your account lives under
      <a href="/cabinet">Cabinet</a>:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>My Templates</strong> — templates you've listed for sale or
        rent (if you're a seller).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Cases</strong> — a way to group the templates you're renting
        for a specific client project, and share a preview with that client.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Finance</strong> — your orders (both what you've bought/
        rented and, if you sell, what's been bought/rented from you),
        with a CSV export and a summary of your Tempasi credit balance.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Profile &amp; Security</strong> — account details and
        password/login settings.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="static-page__section">
    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>
      Reach out any time at
      <a href="mailto:support@tempasi.com">support@tempasi.com</a>.
      If you already have a Tempasi account, the
      <a href="/cabinet/support">Support</a> section in your cabinet has a
      short FAQ.
    </p>
  </section>
</div>
